Project Name: LocalConnect

Tagline: Empowering Neighborhood Commerce, Digitally.

1. Executive Summary

LocalShop is a hyper-local marketplace connecting neighborhood shops (0-20 km radius) to customers.

2. Core Ideas (sequential)

1) Landing & Authentication
- Clean landing page and role-based signup (Customer, Shopkeeper).

2) Real-Time Geo-Spatial Discovery
- Implement `GET /api/discovery` using PostGIS to compute distances and sort shops by proximity.
- Add radius slider (1–20 km) and default location context in frontend.

3) Common Products Library (Crowdsourcing Engine)
- Central catalog of common products (image + description).
- Auto-suggest when shopkeepers add products; allow validated additions to grow the library.

4) Flexible Fulfillment Model
- Support four fulfillment modes: Self-Collect Now/Scheduled, Home Delivery Immediate/Scheduled.
- Add fulfillment selector in checkout UI and persist choice on orders.

5) ACID-Compliant Order Transactions
- In backend, implement transactional reservation workflow: lock inventory row, verify qty, decrement, commit.

6) Shopkeeper Quick Actions
- Inventory quick-adjust buttons (+ / -), library search for quick product add, manual product creation flow, bulk Excel import.

7) Shop & Product UX
- Shop cards showing name, rating, live distance, badges, and stock status.
- Shop detail page with virtual aisle and live stock warnings.

8) Payments & Order Status
- Integrate UPI/cards and support Cash-on-Delivery.
- Order status lifecycle: Pending → Confirmed → Ready → Out for Delivery.

9) Future Enhancements (post-launch)
- AI recommendations, dynamic pricing, route optimization for 3PL.

3. Action List to Update Project (prioritized, sequential)

Phase A — Minimal Viable Platform (High priority)
1. Backend: Add/verify Postgres + PostGIS support; update `application.properties` to use environment variables for DB and enable Flyway when desired.
2. Backend: Implement `GET /api/discovery` that accepts lat/lon + radius and returns shops ordered by distance (PostGIS ST_Distance or indexed bounding box query).
3. Backend: Implement ACID order placement endpoint with row-level locking and unit tests.
4. Frontend: Add discovery dashboard, radius slider, and shop card components; wire to `/api/discovery`.
5. Frontend: Add shop detail page and basic cart/checkout with fulfillment selector UI.

Phase B — Shopkeeper & Inventory (mid priority)
6. Backend: Create Common Products Library schema + endpoints (`/api/library/search`, `/api/library/add`), and support bulk uploads (CSV/XLSX) via an API.
7. Frontend: Shopkeeper dashboard with quick stock adjust, library search add flow, and bulk upload UI.
8. Backend: Flyway migrations for schema changes, sample migrations for geography columns and indexes.

Phase C — Reliability, Infra & DevOps
9. Add Dockerfile(s) and `docker-compose.yml` including Postgres with PostGIS extension for local dev.
10. CI: Add pipeline steps to run `mvn -DskipTests=false package` and `npm ci && npm run build`, plus DB migration checks.
11. Monitoring: Add structured logging and lightweight metrics (Prometheus + Grafana or Application Insights) and error tracking (Sentry).

Phase D — Polish & Advanced Features
12. Payment integration (UPI/cards) and payment webhook handling.
13. AI recommendations + dynamic pricing experiments (offline model then A/B tests).
14. Route optimization service for 3PL partners (batch pickup/delivery planning).

